Key Claim: A corporation is recognized as a legal person when it meets the following conditions:

a) Established in accordance with the provisions of this Law, other relevant laws;

b) Has an organizational structure as prescribed at Article 83 of this Law;

c) Has independent assets from individuals and other legal persons and is responsible for its liabilities with its own assets;

d) Acts on its own name to participate in legal relationships.

Best Supporting Legal Evidence: The conditions under which a corporation can be recognized as a legal person are outlined in the Civil Code of Vietnam. Specifically, according to Article 1, an organization must meet the following criteria:

a) Established in accordance with the provisions of this Law, other relevant laws;

b) Has an organizational structure as prescribed at Article 83 of this Law;

c) Has independent assets from individuals and other legal persons and is responsible for its liabilities with its own assets;

d) Acts on its own name to participate in legal relationships.

